      "id": "6q0kd07",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11.1 Introduction to Computer Networks"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Computer networks enable efficient resource sharing, data communication, and centralized management across interconnected devices.",
        "Networks are classified by geographical coverage into Local Area Network (LAN), Metropolitan Area Network (MAN), and Wide Area Network (WAN).",
        "Network hardware includes Routers (route data across networks), Switches (smart local packet switching), Hubs (broadcasting devices), and Modems (signal conversion).",
        "Network topologies represent physical or logical layouts including Bus, Star, Ring, Mesh, and Tree structures."
      ],
      "id": "yp7oaci"
    },
