    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Hub vs. Switch: A Hub broadcasts data packets to all connected ports (Layer 1), whereas a Switch intelligently forwards packets to specific destination ports using MAC addresses (Layer 2).",
        "Mesh Topology: Provides maximum reliability and fault tolerance through redundant point-to-point links between all nodes, but incurs high installation costs.",
        "Modem Functionality: Performs Modulation (Digital to Analog conversion) and Demodulation (Analog to Digital conversion) for network data transfer over standard communication lines."
